I think that while a volume was uncertain, kubelet retried to mount it again, althrough kubelet may received a not UncertainProgressError, we should not change it's status to unmounted, it should be always uncertain until called unmountDevice successfully

That is what the code currently does, isn't it? If volume was marked as uncertain and on retry it failed with uncertain error again, then it will NOT mark volume as unmounted - https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/pkg/volume/util/operationexecutor/operation_generator.go#L674
Only if on retry the plugin return a final error, then uncertain state gets flipped to unmounted. So, that means - some CSI operation on retry must have returned a final error for the volume and that cause volume be to marked as unmounted.
Unavailable is NOT a final error and will not do that. Something else may have happened.

@gnufied Now the problem is that the  nodeClient.NodeStageVolume and the nodeClient.NodeGetCapabilities have inconsistent action for processing grpc error,  for nodeClient.NodeStageVolume, Unavailable is NOT a final error, it will return UncertainProgressError,  but the nodeClient.NodeGetCapabilities doesn't have the codes.
_, err = nodeClient.NodeStageVolume(ctx, req)
if err != nil && !isFinalError(err) {
return volumetypes.NewUncertainProgressError(err.Error())
resp, err := nodeClient.NodeGetCapabilities(ctx, req)
if err != nil {
return []*csipbv1.NodeServiceCapability{}, err
so the volume device changes uncertain to unmounted  after NodeSupportsStageUnstage failure

Yeah, the volume should stay "uncertain" and not "unmounted" after NodeSupportsStageUnstage failure. Or, in better words, it should keep the volume as it was - if it was uncertain, it should stay uncertain. If it was unmounted, it should stay so.
Any volunteer to fix it?

